# Q: can an author shape ground with the editor's own brush, place on it, and save what they
# Q: shaped — and does the editor refuse to save what the ground refuses?
#
#   MiVic.Game.exe --probe tools/probe/editor.probe --probe-out artifacts/probe/editor.txt
#
# The editor session, scripted: the same methods the panels call, driven without a cursor.
# The session is created on first ask and the screen follows it, so the transcript reads the
# world the author is shaping. See ROADMAP §10.
#
#   - `editor apply` is a brush stroke: the edit is recorded, the passes re-derive from the
#     edited ground, and the count in the list is the count the file will carry.
#   - `editor place` asks the placement rules in the same words a player's construction gets;
#     the refused one is recorded as the reading it is.
#   - `editor undo` pops the last edit and rebuilds the world from what remains, because the
#     world is a function of the list and nothing else.
#   - the save with a refused placement is refused, in the report's own sentence; the honest
#     save comes after the refused placement is gone.

editor tool raise
editor brush 2 8
editor apply -50 -50
editor report

editor tool structure
editor place GunEmplacement 120 120 0
editor report

editor tool lower
editor brush 3 20
editor apply 30 30
editor undo
editor apply 30 30

# The basin is deep enough now that a second emplacement beside it may stand nowhere; the
# report says so, and the save says no, which is the loop the editor exists for.
editor tool structure
editor place GunEmplacement 30 30 0
editor save

editor undo
editor report
editor tool none
editor name authored-probe
editor save

# The mission half: a limit the objective's deadline outruns is refused by the validator,
# in the validator's own sentence, and the honest value saves.
editor mission limit 2
editor save
editor mission limit 7
editor save
